{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And there did not arise a prophet again.</b> Meaning — and none has arisen until now. And its saying ״עוֹד״ (again) means — and none like him will arise again." "And its saying <b>in Israel</b> — this alludes that the entire reach of his prophecy was through the mediation of Israel. Go and learn from this that at times when Israel was being rebuked, HaShem did not speak with him. And our Sages of blessed memory interpreted (Sifrei Deuteronomy 34:10): 'but among the nations of the world,' etc."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:22:40.905411038Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}